dear colleagues dear friends i am  honored to address you at the kickoff of  this new edition of the startup prize  for mobility  accessibility is an enabler of rights  autonomy and equality it is a  precondition for the full participation  of persons with disabilities in society  but for many traveling remains a  challenge due to a lack of accessibility  or assistance  removing these barriers is a cornerstone  of the european commission's efforts to  create a union of equality  this is why the special prize for  accessibility and inclusive mobility to  be awarded in this new edition is  important technological developments  have led to new mobility options and now  it is time to turn the focus on  inclusion so that persons with  disabilities can equally enjoy the  benefits of these new solutions  we need to strengthen existing startups  in this growing sector and inspire the  creation of new ones  innovation should leave no one behind  this is all the more important in our  aging societies a number of eu rules are  in place to make the eu more accessible  last year we launched the sustainable  and smart mobility strategy this year we  will review the rules of passengers  rights and non-intelligence transport  systems to make transport services  accessible for all  over the next decade further progress  will be achieved with our new strategy  for the rights of persons with  disabilities for instance next year we  will set up accessible eu a european  resource center offering also  opportunities to showcase innovation for  accessible mobility  and european commission continues to  reward the efforts of cities across  europe that make their environment more  accessible  with this new special prize for  accessibility and inclusive mobility we  want to showcase solutions that give  better independence and autonomy to  people and smart cities  provide equal access to transportation  services and address social exclusion  i encourage you to join this contest be  a game changer for accessible and  inclusive mobility to build a  barrier-free europe we need you and your  ideas
 

